WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.859
In his youth, Emperor Kangxi faced a great challenge.

00:00:03.972 --> 00:00:07.588
In the south, three feudatory princes commanded large armies.

00:00:07.588 --> 00:00:11.021
Of the three feudatory princes, Wu Sangui had the strongest forces.

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:15.230
In the year 1673, Wu Sangui rose in rebellion.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:18.293
The flames of war soon spread to many places in the south.

00:00:18.293 --> 00:00:21.280
When the news reached Beijing, the imperial court was greatly shocked.

00:00:21.325 --> 00:00:24.525
The young Emperor Kangxi did not back down at all.

00:00:24.533 --> 00:00:27.370
Every day he studied maps, deployed troops, and gathered provisions.

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.053
This war lasted a total of eight years.

00:00:31.053 --> 00:00:34.824
Step by step, the Qing army recovered the southern lands.

00:00:34.824 --> 00:00:38.343
Battle reports from the front were sent back to the capital one after another.

00:00:38.343 --> 00:00:41.961
In the year 1681, the rebellion was finally put down.

00:00:41.961 --> 00:00:44.744
The realm was at peace again, and the people breathed a sigh of relief.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:48.348
As the war subsided, peaceful scenes returned to the south.

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:51.787
After this test, Kangxi became more mature.

00:00:51.787 --> 00:00:54.673
The central government's control over the regions also became stronger.
